By the way, if I modify the "onset" rule from =20

onset <- h / consonant? glide / initial

to

onset <- h / glide / initial

This cuts out {saskrkuarka}, but {bangrblgaria} is saved by being parsed as=
 {ban,gr,bl,GAR,ia} (whereas with the current PEG it parses as {ban,gr,bl,G=
A,ria}).

Is this how we would do it, if we end up prohibiting some or all CgV, or wo=
uld it be more restrictive, like adding "!glide" at the end of the "consona=
nt" rule (which does kill both of these examples)?

